# Copy to `frontend/.env.local` (gitignored). Next.js reads env files from this folder only,
# not from the repo-root `.env`. NEVER commit real keys.

# --- GACS Assistant (the floating help chat) ---
# Anthropic API key, used only by the server route src/app/api/chat/route.ts. It never reaches the
# browser. Without it the chat shows "The assistant is not set up yet."
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# Application budget for the total tokens the assistant may spend (input, cached input and output
# all count). It is best effort, NOT a guaranteed spend limit: set a spend limit on the Anthropic
# account too (Console > Limits); that is the only hard backstop.
#   - Before each call a conservative worst case is reserved; a call that could pass the budget is
#     refused. Real usage replaces the reservation afterwards, so one call can overshoot if the API
#     reports more than was reserved, and later calls are then refused.
#   - Several server processes on ONE machine share the budget safely (file lock). Separate
#     machines or serverless instances each count on their own unless CHAT_USAGE_FILE points at
#     storage they all share.
#   - A damaged usage file refuses all requests until it is fixed or deleted. It never restarts at 0.
# "250000" and "250,000" both work. Leave empty for no app-level budget; anything unreadable is
# treated as 0 (assistant off).
# The running total is saved to CHAT_USAGE_FILE (default: the OS temp folder, gacs-chat-usage.json),
# so it survives dev-server restarts. Delete that file to reset the count.
CHAT_TOKEN_BUDGET=250000
# CHAT_USAGE_FILE=

# --- What is stored ---
# Only the usage file above, and it holds numbers: tokens used, tokens reserved for calls in
# flight (with random ids) and a timestamp. No message text, reply text, user id or address is
# written anywhere, logged, or kept in browser storage; the chat lives in the open tab only.
# Logs carry token counts and error kinds, never the conversation.
# Messages that are off topic, or that contain a password, key or token, are answered or refused by
# the server itself and are never sent to Anthropic, so they cost no tokens.

# --- Who may use the assistant ---
# /api/chat checks the caller's bearer token with the Spring backend (GET /api/auth/me) and rate
# limits per user id. It uses NEXT_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL / NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL; set this only if the
# Next.js server must reach the backend at a different address (for example inside a container
# network).
# BACKEND_API_URL=
# The rate limit is kept in this process's memory (20 messages a minute per user), so with several
# instances each keeps its own count. The token budget and the Anthropic spend limit are the backstop.

# --- Tests ---
# `npm test` never calls Anthropic. To also run the route against the real API (spends a few
# thousand tokens): LIVE_ANTHROPIC_TEST=1 ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=... npx vitest run src/app/api/chat/route.live.test.ts
